WEBVTT

00:07.724 --> 00:11.147
Not even I know the story
from here on, but...

00:15.280 --> 00:17.243
Finally, time for payback against Autumn!

00:18.036 --> 00:20.207
I'm sure the two of you can do it now!

00:39.913 --> 00:41.374
Hey, isn't it bigger than before?

00:41.875 --> 00:44.171
It must be changing phases.

00:51.019 --> 00:55.152
It must've kept eating people while we
were in the book.

00:55.778 --> 00:57.031
We need to stop it.

00:57.031 --> 00:57.949
Yeah!

01:00.580 --> 01:02.207
But how do we do that?

01:02.207 --> 01:04.086
Doesn't this mean it's even stronger than before?

01:07.552 --> 01:10.933
Before, your attacks did nothing if it went defensive.

01:11.184 --> 01:12.394
That's the past!

01:12.896 --> 01:14.482
But I've got this now!

01:15.400 --> 01:18.281
Repair Boost Bloody Enchant!

01:19.993 --> 01:21.412
Deep-Crimson Crescent Moon!

01:22.916 --> 01:26.089
You did it! That worked!
You really do have this!

01:29.387 --> 01:30.598
It's regenerating?

01:31.224 --> 01:32.560
I see.

01:32.936 --> 01:35.692
In that case,
it's Unrepair's time to shine-

01:38.196 --> 01:40.242
Not even a scratch, huh?

01:40.242 --> 01:40.993
Rip!

01:41.578 --> 01:42.872
What are you just standing around for?

01:50.053 --> 01:53.059
Hey, your attack did nothing!

01:53.393 --> 01:56.190
What would you expect from a kid?

02:00.825 --> 02:01.952
Now then...

02:05.835 --> 02:08.674
Powering up Andy and Fuko...

02:13.642 --> 02:16.189
Reconciliation with Victor...

02:19.445 --> 02:23.119
Prevention of Unseen's attempt
at assassinating Fuko!

02:23.537 --> 02:25.583
That just leaves one thing!

02:28.923 --> 02:30.258
Everyone, listen up!

02:33.223 --> 02:38.441
I'm about to draw the strongest Artifact
we'll be using to capture Autumn!

02:38.692 --> 02:40.905
Can all of you buy me time until I'm finished?

02:43.368 --> 02:44.579
If this succeeds...

02:45.205 --> 02:48.127
...I guarantee that you'll be able to catch Autumn!

02:49.213 --> 02:50.675
Sounds fishy.

02:51.050 --> 02:54.139
Sick! It's all up to you, Anno!

02:54.473 --> 02:56.603
Yeah! Leave it to me!

02:57.020 --> 02:59.066
Latla, is that a lie?

02:59.066 --> 03:01.613
Yes. A downright lie, at that.

03:01.613 --> 03:05.495
Big Sissy's fortune-telling is never right,
so it's gotta be true, agoo!

03:05.495 --> 03:06.915
Shut up, Bunny.

03:07.165 --> 03:10.631
In that case, we'll take the profit
after letting them duke it out.

03:11.675 --> 03:14.054
Sigh. That's pathetic.

03:14.054 --> 03:15.473
Pathetic, agoo!

03:15.766 --> 03:18.438
I mean, what'd you expect from a kid?

03:24.909 --> 03:28.041
I really had a strange life.

03:29.961 --> 03:32.675
<i>Lonely... and sad...</i>

03:38.144 --> 03:39.564
ANNO UN
JERSEY / HAIRTIE

03:45.450 --> 03:46.787
And in the end...

03:48.289 --> 03:52.047
I couldn't get the message to Mom.

03:56.682 --> 03:59.061
But, Mom, can you see?

03:59.813 --> 04:01.525
That guy is Andy.

04:02.192 --> 04:07.411
<i>He's Undead and may look scary,
but he's capable of anything if it's for Fuko.</i>

04:08.371 --> 04:09.289
That's Fuko.

04:10.083 --> 04:12.462
<i>She's had a hard life due to her Unluck ability.</i>

04:13.131 --> 04:16.930
<i>But ever since she met Andy,
she's been fighting with courage.</i>

04:18.182 --> 04:21.732
And the small one there is Rip.

04:22.775 --> 04:25.488
<i>He's the person I wanted to tell you about.</i>

04:30.248 --> 04:31.710
I killed her.

04:32.085 --> 04:35.676
No... I killed my little sister.

04:40.143 --> 04:41.688
If I hadn't told that fortune, then-

04:41.688 --> 04:43.776
No, I did the operation!

04:43.776 --> 04:46.698
If I hadn't cut her,
then Leila would be...

04:47.909 --> 04:55.131
<i>He's really kind and cool, but he's suppressed it
ever since losing someone dear to him.</i>

04:57.302 --> 05:00.016
He's even cooler as an adult.

05:00.350 --> 05:03.524
I mean, you always liked handsome characters, Mom.

05:04.274 --> 05:04.984
Just hold on...

05:05.903 --> 05:07.447
I'll show you right now!

05:12.082 --> 05:15.088
Age Rip 15 years!

05:30.243 --> 05:33.249
My body's back to normal?
But this is...

05:34.209 --> 05:38.552
<i>This is the Artifact that Feng used to heal me.
The time-control Artifact!</i>

05:38.886 --> 05:41.933
<i>That's what he drew and used?</i>

05:42.602 --> 05:43.436
You dumbass!

05:44.479 --> 05:47.862
What are you thinking?
When you use that...

05:47.862 --> 05:51.870
...it makes you age ten times
the length of time you manipulated!

05:57.380 --> 06:00.303
How many years did you use?
Hand the Artifact over!

06:00.303 --> 06:02.516
If I use it back on you,
we'll still make it in time!

06:05.731 --> 06:11.701
Don't worry... I'm just going back...
to being alone again.

06:13.580 --> 06:20.051
In order to capture Autumn, Rip...
your power is necessary.

06:22.222 --> 06:26.146
I'm glad I managed...
to meet and talk to you.

06:27.482 --> 06:30.071
The rest is up to you now...

06:31.073 --> 06:34.664
...my cast... of cool heroes.

06:43.431 --> 06:44.182
Huh?

07:12.615 --> 07:13.867
It's her fault!

07:15.119 --> 07:17.792
My child got hurt because
he played with that girl!

07:18.167 --> 07:19.670
What are you going to do about this?

07:19.670 --> 07:21.256
It was an accident, Mom.

07:21.591 --> 07:25.599
I've said this numerous times,
but Fuko hasn't done anything.

07:25.599 --> 07:27.812
The other young'uns said so themselves, didn't they?

07:27.812 --> 07:31.528
That girl is always at the scene
of every incident that happens at their school!

07:31.528 --> 07:33.824
She must've pulled some prank!

07:39.292 --> 07:41.506
You haven't done anythin' wrong, Fuko.

07:42.883 --> 07:43.677
Yeah.

07:46.473 --> 07:48.937
Grandpa, what's this?

07:48.937 --> 07:52.193
Oh? That was your mom's favorite manga.

07:52.193 --> 07:55.617
When a new volume comes out,
I buy it and put it as an offering.

07:56.410 --> 07:59.584
Manga? Can I read it?

07:59.667 --> 08:04.969
Aye, go right ahead.
I'm sure that'd make your mom happy.

08:09.227 --> 08:12.442
Oh, wow... Look at all the pretty pictures.

08:14.947 --> 08:16.618
<i>My parents died.</i>

08:18.997 --> 08:20.499
<i>My grandpa died.</i>

08:23.214 --> 08:26.303
Even then, one thing kept me
from ending it all...

08:27.598 --> 08:31.355
Well, I can't die until this ends,
now can I?

08:34.695 --> 08:36.031
Sensei...

08:54.569 --> 08:57.908
<i>It's regenerating too fast,
how should I attack?</i>

08:58.242 --> 08:59.119
Undead.

08:59.411 --> 09:00.371
Wuzzat?

09:00.622 --> 09:06.551
Who was that man? Why did he disappear?
And why did he turn me back to normal?

09:08.805 --> 09:13.230
I've told you before.
I don't plan on getting all buddy-buddy with you guys!

09:13.982 --> 09:17.196
Did you think I'd help you because I'm in your debt?

09:17.906 --> 09:20.662
That I'd have a change of heart
if you appealed to my emotions?

09:21.121 --> 09:23.543
Well... I refuse.

09:24.837 --> 09:27.760
Sensei called us heroes.

09:28.260 --> 09:30.473
Sensei did so much for all of us.

09:31.517 --> 09:33.688
<i>He used You-Me to guide us...</i>

09:34.732 --> 09:38.907
<i>He gave us the chance to go
to Andy's past to become stronger.</i>

09:39.909 --> 09:41.662
<i>And last, but not least...</i>

09:42.790 --> 09:44.459
<i>He reverted you.</i>

09:47.841 --> 09:51.557
All of these things are necessary to beat Autumn.

09:55.607 --> 09:59.030
Hey, Rip's body's back t'normal,
but he don't look too happy, agoo...

09:59.030 --> 10:00.449
What's da matter?

10:00.449 --> 10:04.499
Well... Rip wants to be a villain.

10:06.336 --> 10:09.677
Otherwise, he'll never reach his destination.

10:12.683 --> 10:19.572
<i>Being a hero means giving up on her.</i>

10:20.030 --> 10:20.657
Rip!

10:22.201 --> 10:24.330
I'll cut up this lug with my katana.

10:24.330 --> 10:27.086
Then you attack the same spot
and make it unrepairable.

10:27.086 --> 10:27.838
Huh?

10:28.088 --> 10:30.301
Latla, you defend the front.

10:31.762 --> 10:34.560
We need you to slip past its barrage fire.

10:34.810 --> 10:37.524
Wait a second!
Don't just casually call me out by name!

10:37.691 --> 10:42.701
Bunny, you're a Restrainer Type, right?
You're on core retrieval duty.

10:43.118 --> 10:44.580
Yessir, agoo!

10:44.663 --> 10:45.790
Bunny!

10:46.124 --> 10:49.673
Hey! Who said you could call all
the shots? We're-

10:49.673 --> 10:50.967
We're...

10:51.511 --> 10:54.182
...able to win.
Without a doubt!

10:57.438 --> 10:58.190
Agoo?

10:58.482 --> 10:59.944
What is that?

11:06.039 --> 11:07.834
Autumn's spiderlings!

11:08.126 --> 11:10.005
They're going into the main body...

11:25.077 --> 11:26.831
This is its Phase 2, huh?

11:26.831 --> 11:29.962
No way... You mean it wasn't already
at max strength?

11:30.296 --> 11:35.557
Oh my, all of you look like
you'd make quite lovely books.

11:36.016 --> 11:37.519
Especially you.

11:38.103 --> 11:40.525
You'll make a good bookmark!

11:42.153 --> 11:43.615
Andy! Below!

11:46.829 --> 11:47.623
Andy!

11:52.507 --> 11:53.885
What's got into you?

11:54.260 --> 11:58.603
Rip, you've been helping me...
for as far back as I can remember.

11:59.228 --> 12:01.609
Rip... you're like...

12:01.692 --> 12:03.153
<i>...some kind of hero, huh?</i>

12:10.042 --> 12:11.796
Oh my, it won't heal...

12:12.839 --> 12:13.841
Mr. Rip!

12:18.726 --> 12:19.687
Latla?

12:20.563 --> 12:21.481
Yeah?

12:22.651 --> 12:24.530
Can we beat this thing?

12:24.780 --> 12:27.744
We'll lose. Without a doubt.

12:32.211 --> 12:38.014
<i>This is the tale of a single boy
who guided a cast of heroes.</i>

12:39.350 --> 12:41.146
Just this once.

12:42.356 --> 12:43.735
We'll see.

12:45.572 --> 12:49.913
<i>This story started when a little boy who loves manga...</i>

12:49.913 --> 12:54.422
<i>...picked up a mysterious pen that showed him
the past and future.</i>

12:58.305 --> 13:03.440
<i>The boy tried to tell his mother
of his visions of the past and future...</i>

13:03.775 --> 13:06.237
<i>...but failed despite his best efforts.</i>

13:09.452 --> 13:14.378
<i>That was because he became the Negator "Unknown."</i>

13:16.884 --> 13:20.057
<i>Nobody noticed him,
he was all alone.</i>

13:20.725 --> 13:27.029
<i>But he never gave up on life partly because
of his mother's desire for him to stay alive.</i>

13:29.117 --> 13:37.466
<i>And because of what he saw that day-
His heroes fighting while facing their bitter pasts.</i>

13:39.470 --> 13:41.642
<i>One day, the boy realized...</i>

13:42.393 --> 13:48.029
<i>...that what he drew as the author "Anno Un"
could be shared with the world.</i>

13:49.616 --> 13:53.123
<i>And it wasn't long before he realized something else.</i>

13:54.000 --> 13:55.168
Fuko, lay it on me.

13:55.168 --> 13:56.547
Huh? Is that necessary?

13:56.547 --> 13:58.759
Yeah, for some luck.

13:59.218 --> 14:01.222
<i>The heroes he saw that day...</i>

14:01.724 --> 14:04.020
<i>...actually existed in real life!</i>

14:04.897 --> 14:07.318
<i>This fact alarmed the boy.</i>

14:07.652 --> 14:09.573
Latla, take care of Fuko!

14:09.907 --> 14:11.284
Please and thank you!

14:11.619 --> 14:13.204
Well, you have some nerve!

14:15.083 --> 14:17.463
<i>Because in his vision of the future...</i>

14:18.423 --> 14:23.183
<i>...Fuko was killed by Unseen,
and this world met its end.</i>

14:26.105 --> 14:27.651
<i>He had to change the future.</i>

14:28.485 --> 14:32.493
<i>The boy's mind was set.
These heroes instilled in him the courage he needed...</i>

14:32.493 --> 14:35.332
<i>...he would risk life and limb
in order to repay them.</i>

14:38.714 --> 14:42.931
<i>With a manga of future information sprinkled in,
he notified them of his existence.</i>

14:43.683 --> 14:46.479
<i>He extracted the manifestation ability the pen held.</i>

14:46.814 --> 14:48.859
<i>And in order to meet Andy and Fuko...</i>

14:49.276 --> 14:53.284
<i>...he created another version of himself,
one named "Anno Un."</i>

14:53.869 --> 14:59.338
<i>As a result, the assassination was foiled.
Andy and Fuko became stronger.</i>

14:59.965 --> 15:04.808
<i>Rip returned to normal.
And preparations were set to defeat Autumn.</i>

15:06.310 --> 15:08.023
Deep-Crimson Waxing Moon!

15:09.400 --> 15:11.029
Full Moonsault!

15:13.199 --> 15:16.665
The wound won't close.
Damn you, vessel of Repair...

15:16.999 --> 15:18.251
Latla, now!

15:18.418 --> 15:19.546
We're busting through!

15:19.546 --> 15:20.422
- Got it!
- Agoo!

15:20.715 --> 15:23.596
<i>Perhaps it was a price to pay
for changing the future...</i>

15:24.263 --> 15:27.311
<i>...but the pen ultimately crumbled to pieces.</i>

15:29.566 --> 15:33.239
<i>He would never be able
to draw another double again.</i>

15:33.908 --> 15:36.454
What now? We can't see it, agoo!

15:36.872 --> 15:40.378
<i>The boy had gone back
to being alone once more.</i>

15:40.963 --> 15:41.632
Don't worry!

15:42.174 --> 15:45.097
<i>However... the boy had no regrets.</i>

15:45.430 --> 15:48.938
Anno, I'm borrowin' your move.

15:48.938 --> 15:52.612
<i>For everything was already told.</i>

15:53.404 --> 15:57.412
Volcano... Unluck Bullet!

16:02.047 --> 16:03.676
What? A finger?

16:04.218 --> 16:07.015
Andy's finger definitely hit its mark!

16:07.015 --> 16:08.978
And that finger is in store
for a stroke of unluck!

16:09.521 --> 16:10.690
So just have faith!

16:12.067 --> 16:15.867
Because we have all that unluck
Sensei gathered for us on our side!

16:24.008 --> 16:25.678
We did it, Andy!

16:25.678 --> 16:27.306
I grabbed it, agoo!

16:35.030 --> 16:41.752
<i>The boy could never see anyone again.
Was he dead?</i>

16:42.962 --> 16:44.925
<i>No, he was not.</i>

16:46.177 --> 16:51.897
<i>Even if no one could actually see him,
so long as people remembered him...</i>

16:52.565 --> 16:54.861
Anno, we won.

16:55.403 --> 16:57.951
<i>...he would be right there.</i>

16:58.661 --> 17:00.915
<i>That was the belief Andy chose to hold.</i>

17:02.669 --> 17:08.388
<i>This is the tale of one hero
who guided a cast of heroes.</i>

17:15.485 --> 17:16.697
<i>The title of that tale being...</i>

17:17.740 --> 17:19.368
<i>"To You, From Me."</i>

18:51.887 --> 18:53.347
Andy! Over there!

18:53.932 --> 18:55.644
Autumn is disappearing.

18:55.644 --> 19:00.905
Yeah. Cuz it lost its core.
The six of us won.

19:05.413 --> 19:06.583
Yeah, guess we did.

19:07.042 --> 19:10.048
Latla, collect the Soul Caliber.

19:10.716 --> 19:11.718
Mr. Rip!

19:11.718 --> 19:14.389
What? We're taking the Artifact.

19:16.520 --> 19:19.567
Thank you very much
for working together with us!

19:20.485 --> 19:23.366
I doubt the two of us could've done it alone.

19:23.366 --> 19:27.499
Even when it looked like Andy and I were
in serious trouble, you came to our rescue!

19:29.504 --> 19:33.386
We were perfectly in sync, too.
That proves we should be working together in-

19:33.512 --> 19:34.931
Unluck.

19:34.931 --> 19:38.605
We can't work together.
I want Ark.

19:39.439 --> 19:44.157
Helping you would mean joining Union, right?
What happens if I do?

19:44.617 --> 19:50.671
Unjustice would uncover my plot. Besides,
your boss Juiz hides and keeps Ark all for herself.

19:51.338 --> 19:56.725
The fact that none of the other Union members knew
about Ark is proof enough.

19:57.434 --> 20:01.191
I have no choice but to steal it...
from under her, by force.

20:03.822 --> 20:05.868
This person must be very important to you.

20:07.705 --> 20:10.586
Yeah... They're my everything.

20:12.673 --> 20:14.051
Big Sissy?

20:18.184 --> 20:20.689
I'm sowwy for stealing your gun, agoo.

20:21.440 --> 20:24.363
No, I'm sorry for hitting you, agoo.

20:24.697 --> 20:26.075
Oh, um...

20:26.701 --> 20:29.206
Are you sure about letting us have Autumn?

20:29.206 --> 20:30.416
Won't you get in trouble?

20:30.793 --> 20:35.761
I'll probably get an earful for letting Sean get killed,
but whatever.

20:36.513 --> 20:39.142
After all, I ended up owing you guys.

20:39.769 --> 20:40.604
Take this.

20:40.938 --> 20:42.692
I gathered what I could.

20:43.192 --> 20:44.821
This is Sensei's...

20:45.154 --> 20:46.281
Undead.

20:47.075 --> 20:50.248
What exactly was he?

20:50.791 --> 20:54.674
I'm guessin' a Negator... Unknown.

20:54.966 --> 20:57.888
A Self-Targeting Compulsory Type, at that.

20:59.433 --> 21:00.561
I see.

21:01.771 --> 21:04.527
Hope you meet them again.

21:04.527 --> 21:05.612
Yeah.

21:05.904 --> 21:08.994
Bye-bye and agoo, Puuko!

21:09.369 --> 21:11.541
Bye-bye and agoo!

21:13.210 --> 21:15.423
Bye... by-

21:17.302 --> 21:19.599
Hah! It got you, too, huh?

21:19.891 --> 21:24.609
Guessin' your body can't keep up
with all that growin' within the book.

21:31.790 --> 21:35.506
You did good stickin' it out for all that time.

21:38.135 --> 21:43.395
No biggie.
It was only about ten years.

21:46.360 --> 21:47.362
AUTUMN ARC

21:47.445 --> 21:50.828
END

22:02.475 --> 22:04.020
Have any black tea?
